        <div id="mistakes" class="scroll-mt-24 mt-16">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mb-6">
            16. Common Mistakes to Avoid
          </h2>

          <div class="space-y-6 my-8">
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Treating the organic seal as a heavy-metal test</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                USDA Organic governs farming, pesticides and handling. It says nothing about the lead or cadmium a pea plant pulls from soil. Orgain and Truvani are both organic, yet Consumer Reports measured them on different sides of its lead level of concern. Judge lead by test results, not by the seal.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Comparing tub prices instead of cost per 25 g</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                Truvani's $29.99 tub and Orgain's $25.99 can look close, but the Orgain can holds 21 g servings and its bigger canister drops to about $2.26 per 25 g. Truvani stays near $3.75 at either size. Divide by grams of protein, not by the sticker.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Assuming every Orgain tub has the same sweetener</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                Retailer listings note Orgain's sweetener and fiber sources vary by package version, and some list erythritol next to stevia. If sugar alcohols upset your stomach, read the panel on the tub you are buying, not a photo from a review or an old listing.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Drinking chocolate plant protein twice a day</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                Cacao adds its own heavy metals on top of the plant protein, so chocolate is usually the highest-reading flavor in any plant line. If you use either brand daily, switch to vanilla or unflavored, or alternate with a whey or egg shake to spread the exposure out.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Counting one scoop as a full post-workout dose</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                At 20 g and 21 g, neither scoop reaches the 25 g many people aim for after training, and pea-based blends carry less leucine than whey. Use a scoop and a half, or add Greek yogurt or milk, if muscle building is the reason you bought it.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

